course: dictionary
lesson: 8129
title: Repetition
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Repetition is when something is done or said again and again. The word comes from repeat, which means to do or say again. «Repetition can build suspense and make time feel slow.» The writer uses the same thing again and again, and that makes the reader feel the wait is long.
explain: Writers choose repetition on purpose, but it can also be a weakness. A repeated line in a poem can build a feeling, like a drumbeat. Too much of the same word or idea in your own writing can bore the reader, so writers try to avoid repetition.
explain: Repetition is useful in other subjects too. In maths, repeated addition such as 4 + 4 + 4 is how multiplication starts, because it makes 3 × 4. In PE, a rep is one repetition of an exercise, so 10 reps means the exercise done 10 times.
fact: Repetition means doing or saying something again and again.
fact: Learning times tables needs repetition.
fact: A repetition can also mean one time of doing an exercise, such as one of 10 repetitions (reps) of star jumps.
fact: Repetition can also mean a thing that is repeated, which is why writers try to avoid repetition.
fact: Repeated addition, like 4 + 4 + 4, is how multiplication starts: it is the same as 3 × 4.
exercise: «Learning times tables needs repetition.» What does repetition mean here? | A short, rude reply | Something that is never done | Something you forget at once | *Doing or saying something again and again
exercise: In PE, what is one rep? | *One time of doing an exercise | A rest between games | A kind of ball | A whole day of sport
exercise: Why might a writer avoid repetition? | It is always rude to repeat | It is the longest word in English | A repeated word is always a mistake in English | *Too much of the same thing can bore the reader
test: «Repetition can build suspense and make time feel slow.» What can repetition build? | Lunch | *Suspense | Fog | Silence
test: In maths, repeated addition like 4 + 4 + 4 leads to which operation? | Fractions | Division only | *Multiplication, which is 3 × 4 | Subtraction
exam: Which word means doing something again and again? | Rest | Lesson | Question | *Repetition
